	<key>readme</key>
	<string>Type the keyword (`mo` by default) in Alfred to browse and search every Mole CLI command, then press Return to run it in your terminal.

Modifier keys
  Return          Run the command
  Command-Return  Run it with --dry-run, which changes nothing
  Option-Return   Run it with --dry-run --debug
  Control-Return  Optimize rows only: flip disk verification for this run
  Command-C       Copy the command to the clipboard
  Command-L       Show the command in Large Type

Commands that can delete files are labelled DELETES FILES in the result list. For those rows, Command-Return and Option-Return always add --dry-run, so a modifier can never trigger a real deletion by mistake.

Configuration
  Open the workflow's configuration in Alfred to change the keyword, to choose a terminal, and to turn on disk verification. Auto-detect picks the first of Ghostty, iTerm2, WezTerm, kitty, Alacritty, and Terminal that is installed.

Disk verification
  Mole skips "diskutil verifyVolume" unless MOLE_ENABLE_DISK_VERIFY=1 is set, because the check can freeze a Mac whose volume has APFS inconsistencies. Turn it on permanently in the workflow configuration, or press Control-Return on the Optimize row for one run. Rows with it enabled say "disk verify ON" in their subtitle.

Requires the Mole CLI. Install it with `brew install mole`. If Mole is missing, the workflow offers to install it for you.</string>
